# These VITE_FIREBASE_* vars are OPTIONAL: the same public web-config values are
# committed as fallbacks in `src/config.ts`, so the app and leaderboard work
# without a `.env`. Only set these to point a fork at a *different* Firebase
# project — an override here wins over the committed default.
#
# These are Firebase *web* config values — public client identifiers by design,
# not secrets. The leaderboard is protected by the RTDB security rules
# (`database.rules.json`) plus anonymous auth, not by hiding these values. Find
# them in the Firebase console: Project settings → General → Your apps → SDK
# setup and configuration. Only variables prefixed with VITE_ reach the bundle.

# Base URL of the Firebase Realtime Database backing the leaderboard. Scores
# live at `${VITE_FIREBASE_DB_URL}/scores`.
VITE_FIREBASE_DB_URL=https://geotracks-d9b5c-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app

# Firebase web app config. Submitting a score also needs the Anonymous sign-in
# provider enabled in the console (Authentication → Sign-in method).
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyC6o9I68tn0KiDNaceuQF1UjKpo4YJRoV8
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=geotracks-d9b5c.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=geotracks-d9b5c
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=geotracks-d9b5c.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=309832762507
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:309832762507:web:00232dc3ff78ae898ac08e

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET IS A REAL SECRET — the only one this repo has ever had.
#
# It MUST NOT be given a VITE_ prefix. Vite injects every VITE_* variable into
# the client bundle, so a rename to VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET would publish
# this credential to every visitor of the site, permanently, in a file served
# from GitHub Pages. Nothing in `src/` reads it and nothing ever should.
#
# The pair below is used by `node scripts/add-community-album.ts`, which runs on
# a maintainer's machine to accept a Suggestion (issue #40, ADR-0005). It uses
# the client-credentials flow to read public catalogue data — no user login,
# free. Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard to get a pair.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The same client id again, this time on purpose in the bundle (ADR-0008).
#
# The review screen at #admin signs the reviewer in to their own Spotify account
# with Authorization Code + PKCE, so that accepting a Suggestion can read the
# album's track list — the one thing oEmbed has never had. PKCE exists precisely
# so a client that cannot keep a secret does not need one: the client id is a
# public identifier and appears in the authorize URL in plain sight. The secret
# above stays out of it entirely.
#
# LEAVE THIS EMPTY FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT. It is set in CI, not here.
#
# Two allowlists we do not own disagree about what a dev origin is, and the
# review screen needs both on the same page:
#   - Firebase Auth authorizes "localhost" and REFUSES IP literals ("a valid
#     domain name is required"), so Google sign-in only works at localhost.
#   - Spotify REFUSES localhost as a Redirect URI ("this redirect URI is not
#     secure") and requires the loopback IP, http://127.0.0.1:5173/geotracks/.
# So there is no local address where signing in to Google and signing in to
# Spotify both work. Set this locally and the screen invites you to connect to
# Spotify and then dead-ends on Spotify's error page; leave it empty and the
# screen says accepting is done from the terminal, which locally is the truth.
# Reviewing and rejecting work fine at localhost either way.
#
# For production, two things have to be true, and neither of them lives here:
#   1. The Spotify app must have the site's base URL registered as a Redirect
#      URI, exactly, trailing slash included:
#        https://georgeharvey3.github.io/geotracks/
#   2. The deployed build needs the value. Set it as a repository *variable*
#      named VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID (Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
#      → Variables); the CI workflow passes it to `npm run build`.
#
# Separately, Firebase → Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains must
# list "georgeharvey3.github.io", or Google sign-in fails on the deployed screen
# — that list governs the Google gate, not this variable.
VITE_SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
